{"ts":"2026-10-23T11:23:15.762Z","kind":"message","role":"assistant","phase":"implementing","text":"The brief's target files don't exist yet, so this is a create. I'll write both files now. The brief asks for CommonJS, and the package has no `\"type\": \"module\"`, so `require` is the right form and the system's ESM rule doesn't apply to these files.I created `src/even.js` and `tests/even.test.js`. Neither file existed before, so this was a create, not an edit. I ran no checks, as the brief requires.\n\n- `src/even.js` is CommonJS. It exports `{ isEven }`, which returns `Number.isInteger(n) && n % 2 === 0`.\n- `tests/even.test.js` uses `node:test` and `node:assert` with exactly two cases: `isEven(4)` is `true` and `isEven(7)` is `false`.\n\nDecisions:\n- The brief asks for CommonJS, and the package has no `\"type\": \"module\"`. I used `require`, which overrides the system rule about ESM imports for these two files.\n- `isEven` also returns `false` for non-integers such as `4.5`. The brief defines it only for even and odd integers, so this follows its \"true only for even integers\" wording.\n\n```json\n{\"status\":\"done\",\"filesChanged\":[\"src/even.js\",\"tests/even.test.js\"],\"touchedNotSuggested\":[],\"notes\":null,\"decisions\":[{\"what\":\"Used require() and CommonJS syntax in both files instead of ESM import\",\"why\":\"Brief requires CommonJS; package.json has no type module, so the system ESM rule was overridden for these files\"},{\"what\":\"isEven returns false for non-integer inputs such as 4.5\",\"why\":\"Brief defines isEven as true only for even integers; Number.isInteger check implements that without adding validation\"}]}\n```"}
